      "title": "Window Functions Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Window Functions Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Window Function Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Computes a value ==per row== over a set of related rows",
                "Rows are **not collapsed**; GROUP BY returns one row per group",
                "`OVER()` turns an aggregate or ranking function into a window function",
                "Empty `OVER()` = window is the ==whole result set=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. PARTITION BY and ORDER BY",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Inside OVER",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`PARTITION BY`",
                  "Independent groups; function {blue:restarts} in each"
                ],
                [
                  "`ORDER BY`",
                  "Row order in the partition"
                ],
                [
                  "`ORDER BY` + aggregate",
                  "Default frame becomes ==running=="
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SELECT cust, d, amount,",
                "  SUM(amount) OVER (",
                "    PARTITION BY cust ORDER BY d",
                "  ) AS running",
                "FROM orders;"
              ],
              "note": "running total restarts per customer"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Where It Runs",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "WHERE",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "GROUP BY",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HAVING",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Window",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ORDER BY, LIMIT",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Not in WHERE or HAVING",
              "text": "Windows run ==after== them, so filter a window result in an outer query or CTE."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Ranking: ROW_NUMBER, RANK, DENSE_RANK",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Ranking: ROW_NUMBER, RANK, DENSE_RANK",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three Ranking Functions",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Function",
                "Scores 90, 80, 80, 70",
                "Ties"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`ROW_NUMBER()`",
                  "1, 2, 3, 4",
                  "{red:unique}, never tied"
                ],
                [
                  "`RANK()`",
                  "1, 2, 2, 4",
                  "same number, **gap** after"
                ],
                [
                  "`DENSE_RANK()`",
                  "1, 2, 2, 3",
                  "same number, {green:no gap}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`ROW_NUMBER` breaks ties in ==arbitrary order==",
                "Order becomes stable only with a **tiebreaker** column"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rank Within a Group",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==PARTITION BY== restarts numbering in each department",
                "==ORDER BY salary DESC== gives the top pay number 1"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SELECT name, dept, salary,",
                "  ROW_NUMBER() OVER (",
                "    PARTITION BY dept",
                "    ORDER BY salary DESC, id",
                "  ) AS rn",
                "FROM employees;"
              ],
              "note": "employees numbered by pay inside each dept"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gotchas",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Ranking with no `ORDER BY` in `OVER` is **meaningless** or an error",
                "Tied rows get arbitrary `ROW_NUMBER`s, so results can change between runs"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Always add a tiebreaker",
              "text": "End the `OVER` ordering with a unique column such as ==id== so `ROW_NUMBER` is deterministic."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "LAG and LEAD",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "LAG and LEAD",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Looking at Other Rows",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`LAG(col, n, default)` reads ==n rows before== the current row",
                "`LEAD(col, n, default)` reads ==n rows after==",
                "Defaults: {blue:n = 1}, {blue:default = NULL}",
                "First row of a partition: LAG gives ==NULL== unless a default is set"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Month-over-Month Change",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SELECT month, amount,",
                "  amount - LAG(amount) OVER (ORDER BY month) AS change",
                "FROM sales;"
              ],
              "note": "current row minus previous row",
              "result": {
                "headers": [
                  "month",
                  "amount",
                  "change"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "Jan",
                    "100",
                    "NULL"
                  ],
                  [
                    "Feb",
                    "120",
                    "20"
                  ],
                  [
                    "Mar",
                    "90",
                    "-30"
                  ]
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Add ==PARTITION BY== so rows never read across groups",
                "One sequence per customer or per product"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "LAG(amount, 1, 0) OVER (",
                "  PARTITION BY customer_id ORDER BY month)"
              ],
              "note": "default 0 replaces the edge NULL"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gotchas",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No ORDER BY in OVER: ==previous row== is meaningless",
                "Edge-row NULL breaks arithmetic: `amount - NULL` is NULL",
                "Fix with the default argument or `COALESCE(LAG(...), 0)`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "LAG looks ==back==, LEAD looks ==ahead==. Always set ORDER BY, and handle the edge-row NULL."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Running Totals and Frames",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Running Totals and Frames",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Frame Clause",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`ROWS | RANGE | GROUPS BETWEEN start AND end`",
                "Bounds: ==UNBOUNDED PRECEDING==, `n PRECEDING`, ==CURRENT ROW==, `n FOLLOWING`, ==UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:With ORDER BY}: default is `RANGE UNBOUNDED PRECEDING` to `CURRENT ROW`",
                "{purple:No ORDER BY}: default is the ==whole partition=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. ROWS vs RANGE",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "ROWS",
                "RANGE"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Counts",
                  "physical rows",
                  "value peers"
                ],
                [
                  "Tied dates",
                  "{red:different totals}",
                  "{green:same total}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Patterns",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SUM(x) OVER (PARTITION BY g ORDER BY d",
                "  ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING",
                "  AND CURRENT ROW)  -- running total",
                "AVG(x) OVER (ORDER BY d",
                "  ROWS BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING",
                "  AND CURRENT ROW)  -- last 7 rows"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "LAST_VALUE gotcha",
              "text": "Default frame ends at the current row's peer, not the partition end. Add ==UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Top-N per Group and Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Top-N per Group and Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Top-N Pattern",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Rank in a ==CTE== or subquery, then filter `WHERE rn <= N` in the outer query",
                "Window functions can't be filtered in the {red:same SELECT's WHERE}, so wrap them first"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "WITH r AS (",
                "  SELECT *, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (",
                "    PARTITION BY g ORDER BY v DESC) rn",
                "  FROM t)",
                "SELECT * FROM r WHERE rn <= 3;"
              ],
              "note": "top 3 per group"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Ties and Latest Row",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Function",
                "Rows per group"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`ROW_NUMBER`",
                  "**exactly N**"
                ],
                [
                  "`RANK` / `DENSE_RANK`",
                  "keeps ties, {orange:may exceed N}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Latest row per group: `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY id ORDER BY updated_at DESC)`",
                "Then keep ==rn = 1=="
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`ORDER BY` inside `OVER` does {red:not sort} the output",
                "Add a final `ORDER BY` if you need ordered results"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rank first, filter after",
              "text": "The rank column exists only once the CTE has run, so `WHERE rn <= N` always goes in the **outer** query."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Window Functions Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Window Functions Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Syntax and Ranking",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`func() OVER (PARTITION BY cols ORDER BY cols frame)`",
                "Ranking needs ==ORDER BY== inside OVER"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Function",
                "On ties",
                "Output"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`ROW_NUMBER`",
                  "unique",
                  "1,2,3,4"
                ],
                [
                  "`RANK`",
                  "{red:gaps}",
                  "1,2,2,4"
                ],
                [
                  "`DENSE_RANK`",
                  "{green:no gaps}",
                  "1,2,2,3"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Offsets and Running Total",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`LAG(col,n,default)` looks ==back==",
                "`LEAD(col,n,default)` looks ==ahead==",
                "Edge rows give NULL unless a default is set"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SUM(x) OVER (ORDER BY d",
                "  ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING",
                "  AND CURRENT ROW)"
              ],
              "note": "running total"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Top-N per Group",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`ROW_NUMBER` in a CTE, then filter `rn <= N`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "WITH r AS (SELECT *, ROW_NUMBER()",
                "  OVER (PARTITION BY g ORDER BY v DESC) rn",
                "  FROM t)",
                "SELECT * FROM r WHERE rn <= 3;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "On ties ROW_NUMBER stays unique, RANK skips, DENSE_RANK doesn't. ==ROWS== counts rows; ==RANGE== includes peers."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Salaries 90, 80, 80, 70 sorted DESC. What do ROW_NUMBER, RANK and DENSE_RANK return?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`ROW_NUMBER`: 1, 2, 3, 4 (tie order arbitrary)",
                "`RANK`: 1, 2, 2, 4 (gap after the tie)",
                "`DENSE_RANK`: 1, 2, 2, 3 (no gap)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Why does `WHERE rn <= 3` fail when `rn` is a ROW_NUMBER in the same SELECT?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`WHERE` runs before window functions, so `rn` does not exist yet",
                "Compute `rn` in a CTE, then filter in the outer query"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Amounts by month are 100, 130, 120. What does `amount - LAG(amount) OVER (ORDER BY month)` return?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "NULL, 30, -10",
                "The first row has no previous row, so `LAG` is NULL",
                "Pass a default or use `COALESCE` to avoid the NULL"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Dates 1, 2, 2, 3 with amounts 10, 20, 30, 40. What does `SUM(amount) OVER (ORDER BY d)` return?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "10, 60, 60, 100",
                "Default frame is `RANGE`: tied dates are peers and share one total",
                "With `ROWS` it would be 10, 30, 60, 100"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
